Subject: queueset: add inert tracing for the formal model

Adds a stable id to queue and request and, when a test installs traceSink, emits one JSONL
record per model action (init, reconfigure, arrive, dispatch, finish, timer_fire, panic)
under qs.lock, after the action's effects. The schema is docs/model-contract.md of the
k8s-apf-formalized repository. With traceSink nil (the default) nothing is recorded or
changed: the only runtime additions are id counters and nil checks. A panic in
finishRequestLocked or in the lingering-seats timer callback is recovered only to write a
`panic` record and is then re-panicked unchanged.
Applies to dbe731cf4b0286d68d743068f251263c70719f3e, with or without 0001.

